# The sdk compiler, built by toolchain builds with the toolchain
# reference's gcc, or Fedora's (gcc-host) without one, on the pos
# reference's glibc. gmp, mpfr and mpc are built in its tree and linked in
# statically, as are libstdc++ and libgcc, so it runs on glibc only and a
# pos build can change any other library under it. The
# build also produces gcc-runtime, which gcc requires; a build does not
# need its own outputs to run. glibc and linux-headers are pos's: from the
# pos reference in a toolchain build. gcc, gmp, mpfr and mpc are upstream
# releases.
pipeline toolchain
build-requires gcc pos-link
requires glibc gcc-runtime binutils linux-headers
with-sources gcc-gmp gcc-mpfr mpc
obsoletes gcc-host
outputs gcc-runtime
archive https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gcc/gcc-16.2.0/gcc-16.2.0.tar.xz e6738e29597f733270731aa90600f37ffdc045079dfc27ec7e8192cc81085c3e
